      "side": 1,
      "message": "I started documenting semantics of NDK callbacks in https://github.com/rust-mobile/ndk/issues/464 and https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/318944941. I recall figuring out what these callbacks do, but haven\u0027t yet added the results to the table and will likely have to extract that again from my Rust wrapping and experiments with this API. Particularly:\n\n1. A user probably can\u0027t reset/remove the callback by setting `NULL` here?\n2. The callback will only be called _once_ (allowing us to clean up state directly at the end of the callback)?\n3. Will calling this function again _overwrite_ or _extend_ an existing callback?\n4. If the transaction is abandoned before being committed, the callback will not be called and the user should clean up any allocs/references in `context` themselves.\n\nSame question for the other callback.",
      "revId": "010b135cb4ebd95ac5c4f3563d5ffdd0ceaba353",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
